Browser-based single sign-on (SSO) for OpenVPN instances using
openvpn-auth-oauth2: users authenticate against an OpenID Connect
provider such as Microsoft Entra ID, including Conditional Access
and MFA, via OpenVPN's deferred "webauth" authentication.

The plugin configures and supervises the openvpn-auth-oauth2 daemon
and integrates it with the OPNsense OpenVPN Instances management
socket without patching core.

WWW: https://github.com/SurfHost/opnsense-plugin-entra-sso
